{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "The 20 public photos of the SAM 2 oracle (training/sam2/oracle.py, N-16; the gate of N-17, docs/13). All are files on Wikimedia Commons whose page carries a CC0 or public-domain tag, read from Commons' API on 2026-11-02 (the licence is the uploader's declaration on the page `page`; check it there before using a photo for anything else). The oracle downloads them, checks each against `sha256` and never commits them; `commons_sha1` is Commons' own hash of the same file. A `sha256` of TBD-after-first-run means the author's environment could not reach upload.wikimedia.org when the list was written (HTTP 429): the oracle then checks Commons' SHA-1 instead, prints the SHA-256 it found and keeps it in manifest.json of the fixtures, and the value is copied here after the first run. If a file on Commons is replaced its hash changes and the oracle refuses it: pick another photo, never loosen the check. Prompts are fractions (x to the right, y down, 0 to 1) of the photo as shown (EXIF orientation applied): `point` is one positive click, `positive_negative` a positive and a negative click, `box` is x0, y0, x1, y1. `prompts_reviewed` is true when they were chosen by looking at the photo (positive click on the main object, negative click on something else, box around the object); false means a generic prompt (the centre; a corner; a box around the middle) that nobody has looked at yet: `report.json` of the fixtures gives each mask's area, so a prompt that finds nothing is seen and replaced.",
